-- title:
--   Translating a full lattice by a finite idele
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $\Lambda \subseteq D$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$. Let $g$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ with respect to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda}$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) of $\Lambda$, the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the pure tensors $z \otimes a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a$ a finite adele whose component at every $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the $v$-adic integers, and write $\Phi(g) =$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda\, g$ for the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ consisting of those $z \in D$ with $z \otimes 1 \in g \cdot \widehat{\Lambda}$, the preimage of the left translate $g\widehat{\Lambda}$ under the inclusion $D \to D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$. The conclusion asserts that $\Phi(g)$ is again finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module and that its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$.
--
--   This is the statement that the class of full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattices in a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra $D$ (finitely generated with full $\mathbb{Q}$-span) is stable under the adelic translation operation $\Lambda \mapsto \Phi(g)$, in the $(\mathrm{FG},\ \mathrm{span} = \top)$ formulation rather than the packaged lattice predicate. It is used in the Cerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the computation of the relative index of $\Phi(g)$ as a product of local indices and in the criteria for cyclicity of the relevant kernel.
